<title>DUBAI: Saudi April oil output/supply 8.001 mln bpd.</title>
<headline>Saudi April oil output/supply 8.001 mln bpd.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's oil wellhead output and supply to the market in April were both 8.001 million barrels per day (bpd), a Saudi source said.</p>
<p>Independent assessments of Saudi output for the month of March averaged 8.13 million bpd, up from 8.05 million bpd in February, both above Riyadh's OPEC quota of 8.00 million bpd.</p>
<p>Saudi Arabia is the world's largest oil producer and exporter and has a sustainable capacity of 10 million bpd.</p>
<p>OPEC quotas are based on supply to the market, defined to exclude movements to, but not sales from storage.</p>
</text>
